  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "15700468",
      "title": "Getting Started with a Custom Hook as a Store",
      "sourceHash": "77a4574a7f055b6f427067b4b9b09d803feb1c2c200a64d745f426d0b8000e5a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.829,
          "end": 5.43,
          "en": "So the context API is not ideal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.43,
          "end": 8.09,
          "en": "But there is a different way you could manage this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.09,
          "end": 10.5,
          "en": "And for this, I'll create a new folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.5,
          "end": 13.54,
          "en": "And I'll name it hooks-store, you could name it just store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.54,
          "end": 16.4,
          "en": "But I already have a store folder for my Redux stuff.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.4,
          "end": 18.01,
          "en": "And I don't want to delete that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.01,
          "end": 19.11,
          "en": "Because now I will build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.11,
          "end": 22.12,
          "en": "my own global state management store and solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.12,
          "end": 24.18,
          "en": "with just JavaScript react",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.18,
          "end": 25.85,
          "en": "and react hooks and nothing else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.85,
          "end": 28.34,
          "en": "and ultimate the context API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.34,
          "end": 32.77,
          "en": "In that hooks store here, I'll create a new store js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.77,
          "end": 34.58,
          "en": "And in that file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.58,
          "end": 37.86,
          "en": "I'll now show you a solution of managing state globally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.86,
          "end": 40.52,
          "en": "with Justwell, React and JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.52,
          "end": 43.47,
          "en": "So let's say we're using that file to manage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.47,
          "end": 46.09,
          "en": "our global state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.09,
          "end": 49.09,
          "en": "And I'm deliberately using a very generic name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.09,
          "end": 51.67,
          "en": "because we'll be able to use this store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.67,
          "end": 54.611,
          "en": "for all kinds of states, not just for our products.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.611,
          "end": 57.23,
          "en": "Global state could be an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 57.23,
          "end": 60.83,
          "en": "Now we also want to have a couple of places in the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.83,
          "end": 63.69,
          "en": "where we can listen to changes in that state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 63.69,
          "end": 67.83,
          "en": "So all that a variable listeners here, that's an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.83,
          "end": 71.51,
          "en": "Please note that both these things are normal variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.51,
          "end": 73.73,
          "en": "in this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.73,
          "end": 76.7,
          "en": "Block scoped so not globally available variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.7,
          "end": 78.49,
          "en": "but only available in that file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.49,
          "end": 81.96000000000001,
          "en": "but they're not tied to any class or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.96000000000001,
          "end": 85.94,
          "en": "They're just in that file. They're also not exported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.94,
          "end": 87.82,
          "en": "So we got listeners, we got the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.82,
          "end": 90.03999999999999,
          "en": "we'll also need a couple of actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 90.03999999999999,
          "end": 91.52,
          "en": "which can be dispatched in depth.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 91.52,
          "end": 93.47,
          "en": "Let's say it's an empty object for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 94.97999999999999,
          "end": 97.16,
          "en": "Okay, so now we got these three things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 97.16,
          "end": 99.08,
          "en": "Now let's create a custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 99.08,
          "end": 102.47,
          "en": "Definitely have a look at the React hooks module first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 102.47,
          "end": 104.47999999999999,
          "en": "so that you have an idea of how hooks work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 104.47999999999999,
          "end": 107.312,
          "en": "and how you would build custom hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 107.312,
          "end": 109.19,
          "en": "So here I'll create a custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.19,
          "end": 112.25999999999999,
          "en": "and I'll name it useStore. And just like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 112.25999999999999,
          "end": 115.18,
          "en": "all react hooks its a function just a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 115.18,
          "end": 118.663,
          "en": "like this. Now in this hook here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 118.663,
          "end": 123.22,
          "en": "in this custom hook I can of course use other react hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 123.22,
          "end": 127.83,
          "en": "So now lets import such a react hook. And there lets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.83,
          "end": 132.83,
          "en": "import the useState hook. Because my goal here now is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.23,
          "end": 137.15,
          "en": "that I have some mechanism that could lead to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.15,
          "end": 139.786,
          "en": "other components to re render, and useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.786,
          "end": 141.777,
          "en": "has such a mechanism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.777,
          "end": 143.48,
          "en": "UseState allows us to manage a state and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 143.48,
          "end": 146.13,
          "en": "whenever we update that state any component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 146.13,
          "end": 148.72,
          "en": "that uses useState will re render.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 148.72,
          "end": 151.149,
          "en": "And you also learned in the react hook section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 151.149,
          "end": 155.11,
          "en": "that if a component uses a custom hook, and that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 155.11,
          "end": 157.9,
          "en": "custom hook uses useState, the component that uses the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 157.9,
          "end": 160.44,
          "en": "custom hook will re render when you state in that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 160.44,
          "end": 162.52,
          "en": "custom hook will trigger a re render.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 162.52,
          "end": 165.03,
          "en": "And that's what I will take advantage of here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 165.03,
          "end": 168.55,
          "en": "So I want to have some state here, in my custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 168.55,
          "end": 171.3,
          "en": "And that state will actually be my global state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 171.3,
          "end": 174.05,
          "en": "So I am using the variable which is defined outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 174.05,
          "end": 175.72,
          "en": "of my hook, and that's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 175.72,
          "end": 178.85,
          "en": "It's defined outside of my hook. So it's global.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 178.85,
          "end": 182.81,
          "en": "It's not recreated when we call useStore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 182.81,
          "end": 186.36,
          "en": "It's not created separately for every component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 186.36,
          "end": 188.11,
          "en": "that consumes my custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 188.11,
          "end": 191.54,
          "en": "Instead it will be created once when this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 191.54,
          "end": 193.88,
          "en": "is first imported, basically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 193.88,
          "end": 196.074,
          "en": "And there after any other file that imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 196.074,
          "end": 199.27,
          "en": "from the same file will all use that same state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 199.27,
          "end": 202.17000000000002,
          "en": "And that's one important idea here we'll share data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 202.17000000000002,
          "end": 204.48,
          "en": "between all files that import from it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 204.48,
          "end": 207.81,
          "en": "And that's not something we did before with custom hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 207.81,
          "end": 210.97,
          "en": "The air, the idea was the opposite that we could share logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 210.97,
          "end": 215.61,
          "en": "but not data now will share logic and data by managing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 215.61,
          "end": 218.48,
          "en": "the data outside of the hook because inside of the hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 218.48,
          "end": 219.82999999999998,
          "en": "it would not be shared.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 219.82999999999998,
          "end": 221.88,
          "en": "It would be inclusive to each component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 221.88,
          "end": 223.567,
          "en": "Each component would get it's own data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 223.567,
          "end": 227.04,
          "en": "But managing it outside of the hook every file imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 227.04,
          "end": 229.57,
          "en": "this file or something from that file gets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 229.57,
          "end": 231.24,
          "en": "the same shared data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 231.24,
          "end": 236.24,
          "en": "So here we use this state and of course we dare forget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 238.23,
          "end": 241.93,
          "en": "our two values, which be can destructure here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 241.93,
          "end": 244.96,
          "en": "But, I'm actually only interested in my set values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 244.96,
          "end": 247.77,
          "en": "So my set state value. You can name this whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 247.77,
          "end": 250.77,
          "en": "But since I have that abstract global state name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 250.77,
          "end": 252.6,
          "en": "I'll just name this set state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 252.6,
          "end": 255.31,
          "en": "And I just have to set state function because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 255.31,
          "end": 258.21,
          "en": "I'm only interested in the second value, India Radio",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 258.21,
          "end": 259.043,
          "en": "state gives me.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 259.043,
          "end": 261.62,
          "en": "So I'm not interested in the current state snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 261.62,
          "end": 264.82,
          "en": "I'm just interested in that second value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 264.82,
          "end": 266.473,
          "en": "So, in the updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 267.32,
          "end": 270.42,
          "en": "Now, why am I interested in this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 270.42,
          "end": 273.052,
          "en": "I'm interested in this, because whenever dysfunction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 273.052,
          "end": 276.13,
          "en": "is called the component that uses my custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 276.13,
          "end": 279.192,
          "en": "will re render and we'll need this later to re render our",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 279.192,
          "end": 282.15999999999997,
          "en": "components when our state changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 282.15999999999997,
          "end": 285.78,
          "en": "We're not there yet but that's why I have this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 285.78,
          "end": 288.95,
          "en": "Now I want to add this function to my listeners array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 288.95,
          "end": 292.98,
          "en": "because listeners should be an array full of functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 292.98,
          "end": 295.57,
          "en": "which I can call to update all components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 295.57,
          "end": 298.13,
          "en": "that are using my hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 298.13,
          "end": 301.03,
          "en": "So that I have a list of listeners, a list of components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 301.03,
          "end": 303.823,
          "en": "are interested in updates to my global state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 305.87,
          "end": 310.18,
          "en": "So we can use listeners push here and push setState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 310.18,
          "end": 313.52,
          "en": "So push a pointer at this function to listeners.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 313.52,
          "end": 316.42,
          "en": "That means that every component that uses my custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 316.42,
          "end": 318.46,
          "en": "will get its own setState function which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 318.46,
          "end": 321.09,
          "en": "is 10 added to the shared listeners array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 321.09,
          "end": 323.31,
          "en": "So this array will grow over time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 323.31,
          "end": 324.89300000000003,
          "en": "the more components we add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 326.68,
          "end": 328.83,
          "en": "Now of course it would be great that if a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 328.83,
          "end": 331.9,
          "en": "is unmounted we get rid of its listeners, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 331.9,
          "end": 335.043,
          "en": "Therefore also use the useEffect hook here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 336.89,
          "end": 341.03,
          "en": "And actually use useEffect here so that I push",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 341.03,
          "end": 346.03,
          "en": "something to listeners in useEffect so this will be ran",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 346.23,
          "end": 350.04,
          "en": "whenever a component uses my hook updates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 350.04,
          "end": 353.81,
          "en": "Now I'll add the second argument useEffect to define the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 353.81,
          "end": 357.74,
          "en": "dependencies and with an empty array this means that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 357.74,
          "end": 360.36,
          "en": "this effect will only run for the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 360.36,
          "end": 363.36,
          "en": "that uses my custom hook when that component mounts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 363.36,
          "end": 364.25,
          "en": "and that makes sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 364.25,
          "end": 366.31,
          "en": "I want to readjust the listener for the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 366.31,
          "end": 367.34,
          "en": "when it mounts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 367.34,
          "end": 370.32,
          "en": "And we can also provide a cleanup function here so that we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 370.32,
          "end": 372.6,
          "en": "remove the listener when the component unmounts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 372.6,
          "end": 375.9,
          "en": "because with this dependency array will simply only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 375.9,
          "end": 377.26,
          "en": "run the effect once and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 377.26,
          "end": 380.06,
          "en": "run the cleanup function when the component is removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 380.06,
          "end": 381.68,
          "en": "So here we have a function where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 381.68,
          "end": 384.06,
          "en": "I want to remove my listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 384.06,
          "end": 389.06,
